<p>I&#8217;ve been using some variation of the same system for my alarm clock since at least <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2011/04/10/alarm-clock/">2011</a>.  Probably earlier &#8212; I didn&#8217;t have a blog before that, so who knows?  As the saying goes: What hasn&#8217;t been blogged about is lost to the mysteries of time&#8230;</p>
<a href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2026/07/22/its-time-to-wake-up-an-emacs-alarm-clock/"><img decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/plugins/wp-youtube-lyte/lyteCache.php?origThumbUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fi.ytimg.com%2Fvi%2FZ-Hzz9-bncE%2Fhqdefault.jpg" alt="YouTube Video"></a><br /><br />
<p>(Here&#8217;s some music to play while reading this blog post (because of the &#8220;I feel like an alarm clock&#8221; lyrics)&#8230;  This is gonna be one of those posts that require a lot of scrolling.  You&#8217;ve been warned.)</p>
<p>My alarm clock idea has been the same since the start, but with a varying assortment of components.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122336" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07260-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>A numpad to input the alarm&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122337" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07259-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>&#8230; and a screen/computer to display time and the alarm.  (And the temperature.  Brrr!)  This particular hardware combination has been going since <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2019/02/24/paperlike-hd/">2019</a>.</p>
<p>So I tap in the time I want to wake up (like <tt>9</tt>) and then at 09:00 it turns on the stereo to play whatever was playing.  I&#8217;m kinda proud of the interface; I&#8217;ve found nothing that is so easy to use in any commercial system.  That is, if the alarm is at 09:00, I just type <tt>9</tt>, and if it&#8217;s at 09:30, I type <tt>930</tt>, and if it&#8217;s at 13:00, I type <tt>13</tt>.  *tap* *tap* done.  (I&#8217;m very good at numpad keying.)</p>
<p>(I guess most people get up at the same time every day, so it doesn&#8217;t matter as much, but I always want to eke out the most sleep I can in the morning, so the alarm time changes every day, basically.)</p>
<p>The problem here, though, is that there&#8217;s too many moving components.  In particular, the system relies on telling the central music server to start playing again, which requires 1) the network to work on the alarm clock computer, 2) the network to be up, (2b) the external network to be up to do DNS until I removed that requirement), 3) the music server to be up, 4) me not having chosen something extremely ambient to be playing, like Music To Sleep By, and 5) me not having futzed around with something that just breaks everything.</p>
<p>Some of these things can be ameliorated, but all of these things have failed over the years, so if I really have to get up, I&#8217;ve started using an Iphone:</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122338" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07261-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Ewww!  This thing has the worst interface imaginable for an alarm clock.  That the interface is geared towards making these long lists of possible alarm times is an admittance of failure: It&#8217;s so futzy to set up an alarm that people choose to have these moronic lists instead.</p>
<p>Not to mention how many times I&#8217;ve lain there for half a minute trying to disable an alarm before it goes off, half awake.  (I wake up five minutes before the alarm 87% of the time.)</p>
<p>So&#8230;  that&#8217;s what this blog post is about: I&#8217;m building a new alarm clock.</p>
<p>I want to keep the good parts of the old system: The numpad.  That&#8217;s just the best input device.  But I want to jettison the rest, which is too unreliable, and have a totally self-contained system that doesn&#8217;t rely on the network or any external components.</p>
<p>I know!  Revolutionary!  A self-contained alarm clock!  I bet nobody&#8217;s thought of that before!  I must be some kind of genius!</p>
<p>Yeah yeah yeah yeah, I hear you&#8230;</p>
<p>Anyway:</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122171" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07101-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I got the components!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122172" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07102-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oh, wow, I&#8217;ve been thinking about this for quite a while&#8230;  <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2025/03/07/i-have-bought-what-may-be-the-best-thing-that-has-ever-been-made/">I got that numpad over a year ago!</a>  But it&#8217;s still very nice.  I bought various small screens while trying to think of a design for the clock, and I ended up with this <a href="https://thepihut.com/products/4-ips-hdmi-square-capacitive-touchscreen-for-raspberry-pi-720x720" data-cached-time="2026-06-27T12:05:41" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cache-2026-06-27-web.webp">4&#8243; screen</a>.  I didn&#8217;t want an OLED one, because of burn-in issues, so I wanted a small one so the amount of light would be more limited.</p>
<p>(My current setup has an epaper screen which is nice light pollution wise, but it means that if I wake up in the middle of the night and want to know what time it is, I have to hit a key on the numpad to turn a light on, and that&#8217;s not ideal, and is another reason to ditch the old system.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122173" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07103-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And I got a Raspberry Pi 5 for this.  You may think that this is total overkill for an alarm clock&#8230;  and it is, but I want to run Emacs on it, and I&#8217;ve just had a lot of problems doing so reliably on weaker Raspberries.  I mean, it works, but suddenly something happens and it&#8217;s out of memory etc, and it&#8217;s just a pain.  Reliability is the point here, so I&#8217;m over provisioning.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122174" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07104-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I also got a light sensor from <a href="https://www.yoctopuce.com/EN/products/usb-environmental-sensors/yocto-light-v3" data-cached-time="2026-06-27T12:05:54" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cache-2026-06-27-web-1.webp">Yoctopuce</a>.  I&#8217;m wondering whether it&#8217;s a good idea to dim the screen when it&#8217;s dark and increase the backlight when it&#8217;s light, but I&#8217;m not sure whether that&#8217;s practical or indeed supported.  But it&#8217;s another fun gadget to play with, so what the hey.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122176" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07106-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>This model connects via Mini-USB, but I see there&#8217;s a USB-C version now, too, which is probably a better idea these days.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122178" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07109-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Uh-oh!  I&#8217;m filling up all the USB ports&#8230;  let&#8217;s see&#8230;  it&#8217;s power to the screen, the numpad, the Yoctopuce, the USB speaker&#8230;  NOOO!  I was also gonna put a Tellstick in there, so that I can also use this as part of my home automation network (the old alarm clock machine is, but that&#8217;s going away).  OK, I have to add a li&#8217;l bus-powered USB hub, too.  That&#8217;s a shame.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122179" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07110-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I&#8217;ve got the cables!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122182" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It works!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122184" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-2-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I&#8217;m not quite sure what I&#8217;m going to use the knobs for.  Well, one is easy enough &#8212; that&#8217;s going to be a volume adjuster for the music in the bedroom.  And then tap it to pause/unpause the music.  The other one&#8230;  I can use to turn the lights on/off?  Eh.  Dunno.</p>
<p>The numpad is, as described, to set the alarm clock, and then the two remaining keys I use for &#8220;cancel alarm&#8221;.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122186" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-4-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So the screen uses a full HDMI connector, and then is USB-C powered.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122189" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-7-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>There&#8217;s all these connectors included &#8212; for if you have a Raspberry Pi screwed to the back of the screen, but that isn&#8217;t going to be an option here.  Instead I&#8217;m going to use cables like this very, very thin USB-C for both the numpad and the screen.  It&#8217;s too bad that there apparently are no USB-powered small USB hubs that have USB-A toward the host (i.e., the Pi) and USB-C toward the devices.  Obviously not USB 3 speeds, but USB 2 would be fine for all of these things.  I guess it&#8217;s just too niche, so I guess I see some USB-C to USB-A adapters in my future.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122192" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-10-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It&#8217;s installed!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122196" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-21-12-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So this is basically the topology I was thinking of.  I&#8217;m building a box where the front of the box is the screen, and then on top of the box, the numpad is sitting.  Then I have that box on the nightstand, and I can tap on the numpad before going to sleep.  And possibly twiddle the knobs to adjust volume on the stereo or something.  (Heh heh, he said knobs.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122325" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07250-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, I think I&#8217;ve got the hardware under control now, so it&#8217;s time to do some programming.  (You can find the software on <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/alarm-clock.el" data-cached-time="2026-06-28T14:18:25" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cache-2026-06-28-web.webp">Microsoft Github</a>.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="839" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122326" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26.jpeg 1233w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-300x300.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-150x150.jpeg 150w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-768x768.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>As a designer once said: &#8220;Futura, centred, and you&#8217;re done&#8221;.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="842" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122327" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1.jpeg 1229w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1-300x300.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1-1022x1024.jpeg 1022w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1-150x150.jpeg 150w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-1-768x770.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But perhaps I can use the currently playing album as a background?  Eh&#8230;  gotta down the opacity on the image a bit, I think, but it&#8217;s not worth fiddling with until it&#8217;s running on the real li&#8217;l screen.  (I don&#8217;t want the screen to be too bright.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122330" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07254-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, now running on the Pi&#8230;  Looking promising.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122333" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-2-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But one think I&#8217;m not sure about is how I&#8217;m going to fasten the screen to the box.  The really isn&#8217;t anything to &#8220;grab onto&#8221; here&#8230;  There&#8217;s the screen, and then a gap, and then there&#8217;s electronics that extend equally far out.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122334" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-26-3-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So&#8230;  er&#8230;  I wondered whether I might stick something between the board and the screen or something, but what?  It can&#8217;t be metal, because that would risk shorting out some circuits.  Hm&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="390" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122343" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27.jpeg 1102w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-300x139.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1024x476.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-768x357.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So for that light sensor&#8230;  I had Claude write a small Python script to just dump the luminance (or whatever) values, and then I can write something in Emacs that listens to that and adjust screen brightness.</p>
<p>But:</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="395" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122344" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1.jpeg 1087w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1-300x141.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1-1024x482.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-27-1-768x362.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>While <tt>ddcutil</tt> is able to talk to the screen, apparently, it doesn&#8217;t get much more than the EDID.  So it doesn&#8217;t seem possible to adjust the backlight after all.  (Lenovo L1950wD!?  Lenovo made the li&#8217;l screen?)</p>
<p>Uhm&#8230;  I could still use the sensor to make the text on the screen less bright.  I.e., add a black alpha channel on top that&#8217;s controlled by the luminance&#8230;  Hm.  Not ideal, but perhaps better than nothing?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122347" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07262-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oh, I&#8217;d forgotten that I&#8217;d gotten these USB-A to USB-C cables.  They consist of a ribbon cable, and then you clip them onto the connectors.  Looking at them now, I thought perhaps the point was that you could cut the ribbon to the required length?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122348" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07263-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But no?  Because the ends of the cable look kinda connectorey&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122349" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07265-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Anyway, I&#8217;ve set up the alarm clock for a test run.  In &#8220;deconstructed form&#8221;.  Just to give it a go in realistic environments to see whether I&#8217;ve forgotten something&#8230;</p>
<p><video autoplay loop muted poster="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/posterigqKgB001.jpg"><source src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/video-jKgaet.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></p>
<p>If you&#8217;re making a light sensor device, what&#8217;s the one extra thing you absolutely have to put on the device?  Yes, exactly!  A blinking LED!  Perfect!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122369" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07278-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But now it&#8217;s carpentry time!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122370" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07279-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>This is the first time I&#8217;ve worked with this material &#8212; it&#8217;s laminated wood with MDF and whole wood things alternating through?  And just 1cm thick, because 1) the thinner the less sawing, right, and 2) it makes the clock a bit smaller in all directions.</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve worked with <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2025/04/29/the-making-of-a-kitchen-clock-a-photo-essay/">thinner wood before</a>, and it&#8217;s just not fun.  It splinters easily, and you can&#8217;t really screw anything into it (and expect it to stay screwed).  (So to speak.)  So I&#8217;m trying this now and see whether it&#8217;s a happy medium between Too Much Work and Totally Splinters All The Time.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122372" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07281-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Errr&#8230;  my jigsaw totally chewed through the wood.  That&#8217;s not nice.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122374" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07283-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So I&#8217;ve got these blades&#8230;  </p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122375" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07284-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>&#8230; &#8220;basic&#8221; and &#8220;fast&#8221; and &#8220;clean&#8221;.  I used the &#8220;basic&#8221; first.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122377" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07290-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Man, that &#8220;clean&#8221; isn&#8217;t any better, especially on the reverse side, which is just chewed to bits.  Am I just using the wrong blades, or is this wood really shitty?!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="374" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122378" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1.jpeg 1971w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1-300x134.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1-1024x456.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1-768x342.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-1-1536x684.jpeg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oh, there&#8217;s something called a <a href="https://www.bosch-professional.com/no/no/expert-hardwood-2-side-clean-t308bf-stikksagblad-2868635-ocs-ac/">two side clean</a> blade.  That sounds like what I want?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122381" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07291-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>A li&#8217;l trip to the store, and I now have some T308TB blades.  Let&#8217;s try one out:</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122382" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07294-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Wow, that&#8217;s some difference.  The cut to the right is the &#8220;basic&#8221;, then to the left is &#8220;clean cut&#8221;, and then in the middle is the &#8220;hardwood 2 side clean&#8221; T308BF.  That&#8217;s incredible.  And it does almost look equally good on both sides &#8212; the other side is even better!  Pristine.</p>
<p>Let&#8217;s do some cutting of the lid for the box!  I&#8217;ve measured so precisely, and&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122386" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-2-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oh.  That&#8217;s not&#8230;  that&#8217;s not right.  Did I really mis-measure that badly?  OK, I&#8217;m following the old adage of &#8220;measure once and cut twice&#8221;, so&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122387" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-3-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Yeah, that&#8217;s really bad.  I&#8217;m off by 1.5cm at one end while being correct on the other end.</p>
<p>Is there a trick to cutting straight with a jigsaw?  <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/mHzx2LME0mQ">There is!</a></p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122388" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-4-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Now let&#8217;s see&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122401" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07307-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I&#8217;ve got these&#8230;  what are they called?  Hand held vises?  Nah, can&#8217;t be right.  Squeezey thingies.  That&#8217;s the ticket.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122402" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07308-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So I squeeze the wood, using one as the guide for the other&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122404" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07310-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But there&#8217;s a lot of mathing involved, since I have to add the width of the guide thing on the jigsaw&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122405" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07311-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Nooo!  It&#8217;s the wrong thickness&#8230;  I want 85mm, but this cut varies between 84mm and 87mm&#8230;  how did that happen.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122406" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07312-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, do it one more time &#8212; cut a &#8220;clean&#8221; bit off, and then guide it to 85mm&#8230;  *phew*  I thought I was going insane there for a minute &#8212; the math wasn&#8217;t mathing!  Things just had to have shifted while I was fastening the vise or something.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122389" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-29-5-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>YES!  CORRECT BOTH ENDS!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122407" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07313-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So there we are: Two sides, 200x125mm.  Bottom and lid 200x85mm.  Or&#8230;  er&#8230;  was the lid supposed to be 10mm shorter?  Uhm&#8230;  Oops, yes.  Grr!  OK, gotta cut 10mm off the lid.</p>
<p>But I want some funky feet for the box.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122408" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07318-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I&#8217;m inspired by the Hollie Fingold box I&#8217;ve got.  It&#8217;s so funny.  So I want some triangle feet.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122409" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07314-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oh, I&#8217;ve got this thing!  It&#8217;s meant for cutting things at an angle&#8230;  but&#8230;  er&#8230;  hm.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122410" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07315-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, I just cut some freehand: As long as they&#8217;re vaguely the same height, that&#8217;s fine, because I can just sand off the tips&#8230;  or rather, I guess I&#8217;m adding some rubbery substance at the tips, anyway &#8212; Sugro or something &#8212; so I can get the feet to the same heights by adjusting the Sugro.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122411" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC07316-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>There!  All wooden bits assembled!  And I changed my mind on the lid length &#8212; I think it&#8217;d be amusing if it peeks out on the front top a bit.  A jaunty hat lid or something.</p>
<p>(That it means that I don&#8217;t have to make another cut didn&#8217;t affect this decision at all!  I&#8217;m not at all afraid of losing any fingers!  *counts*  Nine, that&#8217;s the normal number, I think?  And using 1cm wood made cutting these things child&#8217;s play.  Much less drama than jigsawing thicker wood.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122424" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07332-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Now I just have to nail it all together.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122426" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07334-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I was worried that the wood would splinter when I nailed in the nails, but nope &#8212; I&#8217;m doing a test run with some cutoff pieces to see whether this works at all.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122428" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07336-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It&#8217;s all coming together nicely.  The problem is keeping the nails going in straight: Since the wood is only 1cm wide, and these nails are 2.5cm, if I&#8217;m hitting things at a slight angle, they pop out of the wood on the other side.  </p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122429" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07337-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But here&#8217;s why using nails instead of screws make sense: Using finishing nails, I then use a nail punch to drive them further into the wood&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122430" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07338-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>&#8230; so I can then use filler to completely hide the nails.  Doing that with screws isn&#8217;t really possible.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122436" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07340-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, time to start working for real.  All bits assembled.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122437" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07341-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Bang bank bang and oops.  Once again, a nail going in at an angle&#8230;  *sigh*  This happened three times during the mounting, and I had to pull the nails and do a new one for the worst ones.  Is there a tool to guide or something?  To guarantee 90 degree angles?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122438" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07342-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Tada!  </p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122439" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07344-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>The screen fits!  Wow!  </p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122442" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07364-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, time to swap out the cables I was using during the test run with production cables, which means thinner cables that are angled, for the most part.  So I got some from AliExpress, and&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122443" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07366-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>WTF.  That&#8217;s two angled USB-C connectors, and one has a plug that&#8217;s more than twice as long as the other.  So that&#8217;s one more measurement to take into consideration when trying to find cables that can do the job.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122450" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07373-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But while a new shipment of cables is winding its way from China, it&#8217;s time to do some sanding and painting and stuff.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122451" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07374-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>See?  I messed up one of the corners during cutting, I think.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122452" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07375-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But a bit of sandpapering and it&#8217;s fine.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122453" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07376-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It&#8217;s spackling time!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122454" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07377-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I need to spackle all the ends (to hide the composite nature of the wood), and of course all the nails and stuff.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122455" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07378-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Annoying&#8230;  need several turns with spackling and sanding&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122456" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07380-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And then I&#8217;m just gluing on the feet using wood glue.  I guess I could have nailed them in, too, but&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122457" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07383-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Hey what&#8217;s that outside the window.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122459" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07395-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Double rainbow!  Or triple!  Man.  This alarm clock was born lucky or something.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122463" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07397-1-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Three of the feet actually turned out exactly the same length, but one is sliightly too short.  That&#8217;s a lot better than I had expected.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122464" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07398-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So I added some Sugru-like substance to the short leg&#8230;  and man, that Sugro knock-off from Locktite just isn&#8217;t as good.  For one, it sticks to your fingers like crazy &#8212; I had to do the &#8220;OUT DAMNED SPOT&#8221; for like five minutes to make the gunk part ways with my hands.  Yuck.</p>
<p>Damn monopolists &#8212; Sugru was so good, but then all the big companies launched similar products, so now you can&#8217;t find Sugru in shops.  You just find the inferior knock-offs.</p>
<p>Oh, I see that <a href="https://www.tesa.com/en/consumer/repairing/sugru" data-cached-time="2026-07-03T21:01:09" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/cache-2026-07-03-web.webp">Tesa</a> has bought Sugru now?  Well, they&#8217;re a big company &#8212; why can&#8217;t they make the shops carry it?</p>
<p>Grrr.</p>
<p>Then after doing two coats of primer and two coats of paint&#8230;  it turns out that the lid is now too big!  D&#8217;oh!  I didn&#8217;t take into account the millimeters added by the spackle, primer and paint&#8230;  So now I have to plane off some millimeters.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122539" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07439-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oops!  I went shopping again.  And bought this thing.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122541" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07441-1-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It&#8217;s works!  Got the lid a few millimeters narrower and now it fits again.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122589" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, more cables arrived from China&#8230;  but how does this HDMI connector work anyway?  Do you just flip the white thing up?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122590" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-10-1-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OOPS.  Nope.  *sigh*  The black things slide out instead.  Oh well, I guess I gotta order more stuff from China.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122836" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07447-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I painted the clock black, because my inclination is to always paint things black.  But I wasn&#8217;t careful enough when letting the box dry, and it bonded to some surface and now I have more to fix.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122837" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07455-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But back to that Hollie Fingold box &#8212; I was going to do something fun and whimsical for a change, right?  So how about painting it gold on the inside?  I mean, you can only see a bit of gold when it&#8217;s finished, but some poking up will be whimsical?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122653" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07498-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And&#8230;  are lines whimsical?  </p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122654" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07499-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>They better be!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122657" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07500-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Tada!  Plenty whimsical.  In an orderly fashion.</p>
<p>And then it&#8217;s the moment of truth.  Does the screen still fit after all this painting?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122822" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07673-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>YES!  It&#8217;s totally snug &#8212; I was going to mount it into the box with some Sugro or something (there really aren&#8217;t any good options), but it fits so precisely that I don&#8217;t think I have to do anything?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122824" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07676-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Everything fits!  *phew*  So it&#8217;s time to put the lid on the clock.  I was wondering how to do that &#8212; very few things work well with wood this thin.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122838" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07687-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Like, I got these shelf rests, but the screws here are both too long and too thick &#8212; it would totally splinter the wood.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122839" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07686-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So I cut some bits off and painted them gold, and then I could glue them to the walls and then let the lid rest on them?  Two problems: If they aren&#8217;t totally the right height, the lid is going to be wobbly when I&#8217;m using the numpad.  And if the glue isn&#8217;t strong enough, they&#8217;re going to fall off when I&#8217;m typing.</p>
<p>Ideally I would screw them in, but I&#8217;d have to do that from the inside.  Possible, but&#8230;  I could also use a nail on them, but I&#8217;d have to do that from the outside, and then redo the entire paint job.  *sigh*</p>
<p>But&#8230;  what about a hinge?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122833" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07684-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Finding screws that are short and thin enough locally turned out to be difficult, so I ordered this set.  1200 parts!  Whoho!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122834" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07685-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Look at all these tiny screws&#8230;  just what I need.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122823" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07674-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>OK, test screwing &#8212; do these splinter the wood?  Nope.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122825" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07677-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And I also managed to find hinges that are small enough.  There&#8217;s a huge variety of hinges out there, but (of course) 99.7% are geared towards real solid things, and are inappropriate here.  But these are less than 1cm wide, and so perfect.  The screws that were included were too long, of course, but I had my set now.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122826" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07678-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Huh&#8230;  would it be fun to mount the lid this jaunty way?</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122827" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07679-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>That is, have the numpad be on a slight incline?  Might make it easier to type&#8230;  But&#8230;  nah&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122828" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07680-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I thought it would be fiddly to mount the lid, but it turned out to be incredibly easy.</p>
<p>(Also note masterful paint job.  I&#8217;m a master painter.)</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122829" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07681-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Tada!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122831" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07683-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Yes.  The concept works!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122845" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07690-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And the cables arrived from China this morning.  And this time around I managed to assemble them without destroying them.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122846" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07691-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So connecting from the screen to the Pi&#8230;  but, er, like, I had gotten the Micro HDMI side angled the wrong way.  Even after re-checking five times before ordering.  Gah!  But it&#8217;s OK; I can just have the Pi the other way around.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122848" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07693-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Jamming all the bits in there&#8230;</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122849" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07694-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It works!</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122851" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07696-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And it seems solid and stable enough &#8212; I can tap away at the numpad without any wobbling.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122861" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07702-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I also got a package of these in the mail today&#8230;  What was I going to use these for?  The lid?  Hm&#8230;  No!  Now I remember &#8212; I was going to use them to fasten the screen: Screw them into the wood and then slide the screen down on them.  But that&#8217;s not necessary, it turns out, and it wouldn&#8217;t have worked, anyway &#8212; they&#8217;re only 1mm thick, but that&#8217;s still too thick.  I would have had to have taken that into account (is that the correct tense?) when sawing.</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-122862" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC07700-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Oops, how did that running black paint happen?  I thought I was more careful about sanding those mishaps away&#8230;</p>
<p>Anyway, this is the back of the clock &#8212; I cut out a bit for the speaker.  That&#8217;s probably not necessary &#8212; it would be loud enough anyway.  But what the hey.   And it&#8217;s lucky that the speaker is exactly the same width as the screen, eh?</p>
<p>And that&#8217;s the light sensor poking out at the top.  It&#8217;s possible to break off the tip there (where the sensor is) and then do some wiring between the main part and the sensor, but&#8230;  I don&#8217;t wanna go soldiering.</p>
<p>And the power cable: I was going to drill a hole in the side of the box and just plug it in that way, but because the Micro HDMI was angled the wrong way, that&#8217;s not possible.  But I could get a new Micro HDMI plug&#8230;  I dunno.  Either works, really.</p>
<p>Time for a test drive:</p>
<p><video controls loop poster="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/posterjKuMio001.jpg"><source src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/video-12TXEY.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></p>
<p>It works!  The numpad is clicky and nice, and the menu interface for Other Functions feels very intuitive with the dial knob.</p>
<p>Lessons learned:</p>
